      <div type="apparatus">
        <listApp>
          <app xml:lang="en">L. 1: the text begins with a cross</app>
          <app xml:lang="bg">―</app>
        </listApp>
      </div>
      <div type="translation">
        <p xml:lang="en">Ὁ στρατηλάτης. Θεοδώρου […] δεσπότου τοῦ Κομνηνοῦ</p>
        <p xml:lang="bg">Ὁ στρατηλάτης. Θεοδώρου […] δεσπότου τοῦ Κομνηνοῦ</p>
        <p xml:lang="en">Stratelates. (Seal of) Theodoros Komnenos, despotes</p>
        <p xml:lang="bg">―</p>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary" subtype="text">
        <p xml:lang="en">Following the arrangement of letters within the available space, as well as their alignment, it becomes clear that between the name, which ends in the second row, and the title, which probably begins in the third row, there is enough space for two letters (or more, if there is a ligature). A logical guess would be the article τοῦ.</p>
        <p xml:lang="bg">―</p>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary" subtype="footnotes">
        <p xml:lang="en">On the excavation, see Rabovyanov 2010, p. 103-122</p>
        <p xml:lang="bg">―</p>
      </div>
